<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indian subcontinent</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indian subcontinent is the large region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a> comprising present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, Bangladesh, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> and neighbouring lands. It has been home to empires such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. Its trade and wealth linked it to powers including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> extended its conquests into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sind">Sind</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent.jpg" alt="Indian subcontinent" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeet Dev (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_Subcontinent_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
